nt:*\n        Title: Unified High-Risk Event Logging Framework\n        What: A standardized software library providing consistent automatic event recording across all high-risk AI projects.\n        How: The lab will develop a centralized API that captures timestamps, system states, and user identities into a secure, immutable database.\n        Why: It guarantees technical compliance with Article 12 while reducing the engineering burden on individual research teams.\n        (Word count check: ~60 words) - *Wait, need to be between 60-110.* Let's expand slightly.\n\n    *   *Proposal 1 Expanded:*\n        Title: Unified High-Risk Event Logging Framework\n        What: A standardized software library providing consistent automatic event recording across all high-risk AI projects in the lab.\n        How: We will develop a centralized API that captures timestamps, system states, and user identities into a secure, immutable database for every execution. This tool will be integrated into our core development environment as a mandatory dependency for high-risk systems.\n        Why: It guarantees technical compliance with Article 12 while reducing the engineering burden on individual research teams.\n        (Word count: ~85 words). *Good.*\n\n    *   *Proposal 2 Refinement:*\n        Title: Dynamic Technical Documentation Pipeline\n        What: An automated system that generates and maintains real-time technical documentation for model development and validation.\n        How: We will implement version control for datasets and hyperparameters linked to a compliance dashboard that tracks the entire AI lifecycle. This pipeline will automatically log training processes, testing results, and risk management decisions as they occur.\n        Why: This ensures our records are always up to date and comprehensive, mitigating the risk of institutional failure during regulatory audits.\n        (Word count: ~85 words). *Good.*\n\n    *   *Proposal 3 Refinement:*\n        Title