        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"To maintain prototyping speed, we must treat Article 12 as a systems engineering challenge rather than a series of manual tasks for researchers. We should develop modular, 'plug-and-play' logging utilities that can be integrated into any model pipeline without requiring the developer to write custom telemetry code. By automating the capture of timestamps and input data, we ensure technical viability and compliance while keeping our development cycles lean.\",\n  \"stance\": 40,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Unified Logging Middleware Framework\",\n      \"what\": \"A standardized API and set of wrappers that automatically capture event logs, timestamps, and input references across different AI architectures. It creates a consistent telemetry layer for all high-risk systems.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will develop a shared internal library that intercepts model calls to log the required Article 12 metadata into a centralized, immutable database.\",\n      \"why\": \"This decouples compliance logic from core model development, maintaining our rapid prototyping speed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Automated Technical Documentation Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"A system that auto-generates technical documentation and version-controlled logs directly from the training and deployment pipelines. This transforms live metadata into regulatory records.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will integrate existing experiment tracking tools with custom scripts to export compliance-ready reports in real-time as models evolve through their lifecycle.\",\n      \"why\": \"It eliminates manual record-keeping, reducing human error and administrative overhead for the engineering team.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"High-Risk Traceability Module for Biometric Systems\",\n      \"what\": \"A specialized auditing layer designed specifically to handle the strict Annex III requirements regarding database references and natural person