        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab should view these requirements not as a bureaucratic hurdle, but as a mandate to formalize our provenance and observability pipelines. By integrating automatic logging and comprehensive documentation into the early stages of R&D, we ensure that our frontier models remain deployable within the EU market. We must transition from ad-hoc experimentation records to a standardized system of traceability that satisfies both scientific rigor and legal compliance.\",\n  \"stance\": 25,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Unified Automated Event Logging Architecture\",\n      \"what\": \"An internal software library that automatically captures system states, timestamps, and input-output pairs for all high-risk models. It provides a standardized API for event recording across diverse architectures.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will integrate this middleware into our training and inference pipelines to create immutable logs. This ensures consistency across different research teams regardless of the specific model being developed.\",\n      \"why\": \"It removes the manual burden of compliance from researchers while guaranteeing regulatory readiness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Forensic Interpretability for Post-Market Monitoring\",\n      \"what\": \"A research project focused on developing methods to reconstruct a model's decision path using the sparse logs required by Article 12. It aims to turn raw logs into actionable scientific insights.\",\n      \"how\": \"The team will apply counterfactual analysis and attention mapping to existing log data to identify risk triggers. We will then publish these methodologies in top-tier AI venues.\",\n      \"why\": \"It advances the scientific frontier of interpretability while directly satisfying regulatory requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Living Technical Documentation Pipeline\",\n      \"what\": \"A dynamic documentation system that synchronizes model