peline\n        What: An integrated system that automatically captures training metadata, data lineage, and versioning for all high-risk models.\n        How: We will implement an automated wrapper around our compute cluster that logs every epoch's parameters and dataset hashes to a centralized ledger.\n        Why: This ensures the technical documentation remains up to date without diverting researcher focus from core experimentation. (68 words) - *Good.*\n\n    *   *Proposal 2 check:*\n        Title: Transparent Event-Logging Research Initiative\n        What: A research project focused on creating \"interpretable logs\" that translate latent system states into human-comprehensible event records.\n        How: The team will develop novel probing mechanisms to record the internal decision-paths of models during high-risk operations.\n        Why: This transforms a regulatory burden into an opportunity to advance the scientific frontier of AI explainability and safety. (67 words) - *Good.*\n\n    *   *Proposal 3 check:*\n        Title: Standardized Scientific Documentation Framework\n        What: A unified set of documentation templates that align peer-review standards with EU AI Act record-keeping requirements.\n        How: We will create modular templates for reporting capabilities and limitations that researchers fill out during the model validation phase.\n        Why: It streamlines the transition from experimental prototype to compliant system by unifying academic and regulatory reporting needs. (65 words) - *Good.*",
