roposal 1 Word Count check:*\n        - title: Unified Logging Middleware Framework (4 words)\n        - what: A shared software library that provides standardized logging templates for all high-risk AI projects. (15 words)\n        - how: We will task the infrastructure team to build a set of APIs that automatically capture timestamps, input hashes, and database references across different model architectures. (26 words)\n        - why: This prevents redundant effort by researchers and ensures consistent compliance across diverse projects. (14 words)\n        - Total: ~59 words. *Slightly under.* Let's expand slightly to get into the 60-110 range.\n    *   *Proposal 2 Word Count check:*\n        - title: Automated Compliance Documentation Pipeline (4 words)\n        - what: A system that automatically converts technical logs into the formal technical documentation required for EU regulators. (17 words)\n        - how: We will implement a CI/CD trigger that generates comprehensive compliance reports whenever a model is promoted to testing or deployment stages. (23 words)\n        - why: This reduces the administrative burden on scientists and optimizes our resource allocation toward research rather than paperwork. (18 words)\n        - Total: ~62 words. *Good.*\n    *   *Proposal 3 Word Count check:*\n        - title: High-Risk Traceability Database Interface (5 words)\n        - what: A specialized data layer designed specifically to track input matches and human verification identities for Annex III systems. (18 words)\n        - how: We will develop a secure, immutable audit log that links specific search queries to the exact database version used during the match process. (24 words)\n        - why: This ensures we meet the strictest requirements of Article 12(3) without compromising the performance of our primary AI models. (19 words)\n        - Total: ~66 words. *Good.*\n\n    *   *Refining Proposal 1 for word count:*\n        - title: Unified Logging Middlewar