  *Determining Stance:* 0 = no change, 100 = total overhaul.\n        *   The *agenda* (what we research) doesn't need a total overhaul, but the *how* (the engineering pipeline) needs a moderate shift. It's not changing our scientific goals, just the scaffolding.\n        *   Score: ~25-30. Let's go with 25. It's an infrastructural change, not a research direction change.\n\n    *   *Proposal 1: Infrastructure/Middleware.* (Focus on automation).\n        *   Title: Universal Logging Middleware.\n        *   What: A standardized API wrapper that automatically captures system events, input matches, and timestamps for all high-risk models.\n        *   How: We will implement this as a shared library integrated into our model serving templates to ensure consistent data capture across projects.\n        *   Why: This removes the burden of manual logging from developers while guaranteeing regulatory consistency.\n\n    *   *Proposal 2: Tooling/Provenance.* (Focus on data lineage).\n        *   Title: Automated Provenance Tracking System.\n        *   What: A version-controlled metadata store that links specific model weights to their training datasets and validation logs.\n        *   How: By integrating DVC or MLflow with our CI/CD pipeline, we can automatically snapshot the reference databases used for each run.\n        *   Why: It satisfies the requirement for traceability of input data and reference databases without manual documentation.\n\n    *   *Proposal 3: Validation/Testing.* (Focus on the \"verification\" part of Article 12(3)(d)).\n        *   Title: Human-in-the-Loop Audit Interface.\n        *   What: A lightweight UI for experts to review and sign off on AI search matches as required by Annex III.\n        *   How: We will build a standardized verification portal that logs the identity and timestamp of the natural person confirming the result.\n        *   Why: This transforms a regulatory hurdle into a streamlined technical workflow for human-AI collabor