ving Identity Logging Framework\",\n      \"what\": \"An investigation into using zero-knowledge proofs or secure hashing to log human verification without storing raw personal identifiers. This targets the identification requirement in Article 12(3)(d).\",\n      \"how\": \"We will prototype an authentication layer that records a cryptographic commitment of the verifier's identity instead of plain text. We will then validate this method against GDPR data minimization principles.\",\n      \"why\": \"This resolves the inherent tension between EU AI Act traceability and strict European data privacy mandates.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
