      "message": {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "{\n  \"reasoning\": \"The lab must transition from an academic mindset of flexible experimentation to an industrialized R&D approach centered on 'compliance by design.' We cannot risk the catastrophic fines or market bans associated with non-compliance, especially regarding high-risk systems where traceability is mandatory. Consequently, our technical architecture must be updated to treat logging and documentation not as afterthoughts, but as core functional requirements of every project.\",\n  \"stance\": 35,\n  \"proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Unified Traceability Logging Framework\",\n      \"what\": \"A centralized API and database architecture that automatically captures event logs across all high-risk AI model lifecycles. This system will standardize how timestamps and operational events are recorded.\",\n      \"how\": \"Our software engineers will develop a middleware layer that hooks into existing training and inference pipelines to record data references and system states. This framework will be integrated into the standard development kit for all researchers.\",\n      \"why\": \"It ensures systemic compliance across diverse research teams while eliminating the risk of human error in manual logging.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"High-Risk AI Documentation Protocol\",\n      \"what\": \"A standardized template and mandatory review cycle for technical documentation as required by Recital 71. This focuses on documenting algorithms, training data, and validation processes.\",\n      \"how\": \"We will implement a compliance gate at each development milestone where researchers must submit updated technical dossiers to a secure repository. A dedicated auditor will verify these records before the project can proceed to the next phase.\",\n      \"why\": \"This prevents the loss of critical institutional knowledge necessary to pass regulatory audits and maintain our market reputation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Human-in-the-Loop Verification Audit System\",\n      \"what\": \"A specialized logging module for systems under Annex III that records the identities of natural persons verifying AI results. It specifically tracks the match between input data and reference databases.\",\n      \"how\": \"The lab will build a secure authentication interface that requires a digital signature whenever a human verifier approves or rejects a system output. This interaction will be timestamped and linked to the specific input data used.\",\n      \"why\": \"This directly satisfies the strict legal requirements of Article 12(3) to avoid severe liability in biometric or high-risk identification use cases.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
