ernal SDK for event logging that handles timestamps and metadata automatically.\n    *   *Proposal 2: Automated Documentation Pipeline.* A tool that extracts hyperparameters, dataset versions, and architecture details directly from code/configs into the required technical documentation format.\n    *   *Proposal 3: Compliance-Aware Sandbox Environment.* An orchestration layer (like a modified Kubernetes or MLflow setup) that automatically captures input/output pairs and reference database snapshots for high-risk experiments.\n\n    *   *Proposal 1:*\n        *   Title: Unified Telemetry SDK\n        *   What: A standardized Python library providing a common API for all event logging requirements across the lab's projects.\n        *   How: We will implement a wrapper around existing logging frameworks that automatically injects required metadata like timestamps and user IDs.\n        *   Why: It ensures consistency without slowing down researchers who can just call a simple function.\n\n    *   *Proposal 2:*\n        *   Title: Auto-Doc Generation Engine\n        *   What: A tool that automatically scrapes model configs, data manifests, and training logs to populate technical documentation.\n        *   How: We will integrate hooks into the CI/CD pipeline that export metadata into a structured, human-readable compliance format.\n        *   Why: It eliminates the manual toil of record-keeping during rapid prototyping cycles.\n\n    *   *Proposal 3:*\n        *   Title: Immutable Provenance Ledger\n        *   What: A centralized database for storing snapshots of reference databases and input data matched in high-risk systems.\n        *   How: We will build a versioned storage layer that links specific model inference calls to the exact state of the underlying data.\n        *   Why: This satisfies Article 12(3) requirements for traceability while providing engineers with perfect debugging snapshots.\n\n    *   Role: Dev Engineer? Yes.\n    *   Reasoning (3-5 sentences)? Yes.\n    *   Stance (0-100)? Yes.\n    *   Exactly 3 distinct proposals? Yes.\n    *   Proposal format (Title, What, How, Why)? Yes.\n    *   Length constraint per proposal (60-110 words)? Let's check.\n        *   Prop 1: ~65 words.\n        *   Prop 2: ~70 words.\n        *   Prop 3: ~75 words.\n    *   No bullet lists inside fields? Yes. Plain prose? Yes.",
