d (c)).\n    *   *Idea 3: Automated Compliance Monitoring tool.* An internal dashboard that verifies if a prototype is meeting these logging requirements before it's considered \"deployment-ready.\"\n\n    *   *Proposal 1:*\n        *   Title: Standardized Logging Middleware Framework.\n        *   What: A universal API for all high-risk prototypes to automatically capture events and timestamps.\n        *   How: Develop a shared library that wraps model calls to log inputs, outputs, and session metadata consistently across different projects.\n        *   Why: It reduces the engineering burden on individual researchers while ensuring regulatory compliance.\n\n    *   *Proposal 2:*\n        *   Title: Immutable Versioning and Data Lineage System.\n        *   What: A system to map specific AI inferences back to their exact training set and reference database versions.\n        *   How: Integrate a hashing mechanism that stores the unique identifier of the reference database alongside every high-risk system log entry.\n        *   Why: This fulfills the traceability requirements for Annex III systems without requiring manual record-keeping.\n\n    *   *Proposal 3:*\n        *   Title: Compliance Verification CI/CD Gate.\n        *   What: An automated testing suite that checks if a prototype's logging capabilities meet Article 12 standards before release.\n        *   How: Create a set of synthetic test cases that verify the presence and accuracy of required logs during the build process.\n        *   Why: It prevents compliance failures from reaching late-stage development, preserving prototyping speed.\n\n    *   Role maintained? Yes (Dev Engineer focus on viability/speed).\n    *   Reasoning 3-5 sentences? Yes.\n    *   Score 0-100? Yes.\n    *   Exactly 3 proposals? Yes.\n    *   Distinct? Yes (Middleware, Data Lineage, Testing Gate).\n    *   Title max 10 words? Yes.\n    *   What 1-2 sentences? Yes.\n    *   How 1-2 sentences? Yes.\n    *   Why 1 sentence? Yes.