tic compliance.\n    *   *Idea 2: Governance/Process.* Establish a technical documentation protocol to map R&D milestones to Article 12 requirements, ensuring the \"lifetime\" records are maintained.\n    *   *Idea 3: Specialized Tooling (for Annex III).* Develop specific software modules for biometric/identification systems to handle the precise data recording required by Article 12(3).\n\n    *   *Proposal 1:*\n        *   Title: Unified Traceability Logging Framework\n        *   What: A standardized software library that automatically records system events and metadata across all high-risk AI projects.\n        *   How: The engineering team will develop a middleware layer that integrates with our existing model pipelines to log timestamps, inputs, and versioning automatically.\n        *   Why: This minimizes the risk of human error in compliance and protects us from regulatory fines.\n\n    *   *Proposal 2:*\n        *   Title: Compliance-Integrated R&D Lifecycle Protocol\n        *   What: A revised operational manual that mandates technical documentation updates at every stage of model development.\n        *   How: We will implement a mandatory gated review process where researchers must submit record-keeping logs before moving from testing to validation phases.\n        *   Why: It ensures the institutional survival by creating an audit trail for EU regulators.\n\n    *   *Proposal 3:*\n        *   Title: Annex III Precision Audit Module\n        *   What: A specialized data capture tool tailored specifically for systems used in biometric identification or similar high-risk categories.\n        *   How: We will build a secure database interface that explicitly links input matches to the specific reference databases and human verifiers involved.\n        *   Why: This directly satisfies the most stringent requirements of Article 12(3) to maintain our market reputation for precision.\n\n    *   Reasoning: 3-5 sentences? Yes.\n    *   Score: 0-100? Yes.\n    *