e.*\n        *   What: A unified library for all high-risk projects to handle event logging automatically.\n        *   How: Implement an internal Python package that wraps model calls and logs metadata, timestamps, and inputs to a centralized secure database.\n        *   Why: This removes the manual burden from researchers and ensures consistency across different prototypes.\n\n    *   *Idea 2: Automated Technical Documentation Generator.*\n        *   What: A tool that extracts hyperparameters, dataset versions, and architecture details directly from code/config into a compliant document.\n        *   How: Integrate with MLflow or Weights & Biases to automatically generate the \"technical documentation\" required by Recital 71 upon every model registration.\n        *   Why: It eliminates the manual writing of reports which typically slows down the transition from R&D to deployment.\n\n    *   *Idea 3: High-Risk Compliance Validation Suite (CI/CD).*\n        *   What: An automated test suite in the CI/CD pipeline that checks if a model's logging hooks are functioning before it can be tagged as \"deployment ready.\"\n        *   How: Create synthetic tests that trigger specific events and verify that the corresponding logs are correctly recorded according to Article 12 specifications.\n        *   Why: It prevents \"compliance regressions\" and ensures technical viability without needing a manual audit for every iteration.\n\n    *   Check word counts (60-110 per proposal).\n    *   Ensure no bullet lists inside fields.\n    *   Plain prose.\n    *   Verify role consistency.",
