eck word counts for proposals.\n    *   Check sentence counts for reasoning.\n    *   Ensure no bullet points inside fields.\n    *   Verify persona (Compliance Officer).\n    *   Verify numerical range (0-100).\n\n    *Proposal 1 Word Count Check:*\n    Title: Unified Traceability Logging Framework (4 words)\n    What: A standardized API for all high-risk projects to automatically record event logs, timestamps, and input data matches. (18 words)\n    How: We will integrate a centralized telemetry service into our model deployment pipeline that enforces the logging schema required by Article 12. (21 words)\n    Why: It ensures systemic compliance across all projects without relying on individual researcher diligence. (14 words)\n    Total: ~57 words. *Need to expand slightly to hit 60-110.*\n    *Adjustment:* \"A standardized, institution-wide API for all high-risk AI projects to automatically record event logs, timestamps, and specific input data matches.\" (21 words). \"We will integrate a centralized telemetry service into our model deployment pipeline that enforces the mandatory logging schema required by Article 12. This system will be hardcoded into the base environment.\" (30 words).\n    New Total: ~69 words. Perfect.\n\n    *Proposal 2 Word Count Check:*\n    Title: Dynamic Technical Documentation Pipeline (4 words)\n    What: An automated system that generates living technical documents by pulling metadata directly from training logs and version control systems. (20 words)\n    How: We will implement a CI/CD trigger that automatically updates the compliance dossier whenever model hyperparameters, datasets, or architectures are modified. (21 words)\n    Why: This minimizes human error and prevents the risk of outdated documentation during regulatory audits. (15 words)\n    Total: ~60 words. Perfect.\n\n    *Proposal 3 Word Count Check:*\n    Title: High-Risk System Monitoring Dashboard (5 words)\n    What: A real-time observability tool designed to flag eve